# Build-context excludes for every image (the build context is the project root, and a
# `COPY . .` copies whatever is left). Two jobs: keep secrets and local data out of every
# layer, and keep host-only trees out so an edit to them never invalidates a build.
#
# Every pattern in .gitignore but its generated files is here too, matching the same
# paths: an unanchored git pattern matches at any depth, so it is written `**/` here, and
# its exceptions come after it, because the last match wins. The framework's template
# tests hold the two files together, so a secret-bearing pattern added to one and not the
# other fails there rather than in an image.
#
# Never excluded: .terp-dist/, the pre-release packages a checkout vendors. The images
# install from it.

# Secrets: compose's own variable file and its variants, and the rendered app-declared
# variables, per service too (`.app.worker.env`). The tracked examples stay.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.example.jinja
**/.app.env
**/.app.*.env

# Local data: development databases and SQLite's sidecar files, and the files
# capability's storage root outside Docker.
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-*
var

# Dependency trees and caches: every image installs its own, from the lock.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.eslintcache

# Build and test output.
**/dist
conformance/test-results
conformance/playwright-report
frontend/coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov

# Version control and the CI definitions: no image reads them.
.git
.github
